 "notes_text": "A carousel, the most hummable of the four. Every hook bar opens with a chromatic lower-neighbour shiver on the soft beat 1 (G-F#-G over i, F-E-F over V7) followed by two plain quarters, so the bar sounds 'shiver-a-a': the original's pulse kept, with a new figure in the 'u'. The harmony is the most literal twin, i <-> V7 every bar, but over a root-position C-G oom (not C-D) and with G/Eb/F/D in the top line instead of the original's C/Eb/D/F u-a-a. Middle spins: a two-beat swirl C-Eb-F | G-F-Eb (bar 5), then a run C-Db-F through the Neapolitan chord into the cry, Ab5 at 7.9 s, which falls a semitone to G as V7 arrives (Ab->G over N6->V, reached from below by the arpeggio, not by the original's +8 leap). The shiver returns over the tonic (bar 8); the cadence uses vii°7/V with the melodic augmented second Eb-F# for the old-world colour, the tonic arrives a triplet early and is held over the waltz, with a diminished seventh under it at the end. Range B4-Ab5 (9 semitones), 96 % of the notes inside a fifth, 56 % triplets."
